# Issue: BinData wrote a Map or Set by iterating it, so entries keyed on Id or
# IType (the IPackage type-function cache, a module's method-conflict table)
# came out in string-intern order, which depends on the names already seen.
# Fix: each key is encoded on its own and the entries follow those encodings.
# Pull request: https://github.com/MatX-inc/bsc/pull/189
# Probe: SerOrder's two structs give its type-function cache two entries keyed
# by name; SerOrderScramble interns the names in the other order, and the
# one-shot and batched .bo dumps must agree, hash included.

batching_bo_pair SerOrder.bsv SerOrderRoot.bsv SerOrderScramble.bsv
